anthropic_raw_latex:
\begin{thm}
The probability $p(X,k)$ that an arbitrary collection of $k$ quartets is decisive has the property \[p(X,k) \geq \frac{\sum\limits_{i=1}^{n-3} (-1)^{i+1}{{n-3} \choose i}{{|Q_T|-i(n-3)} \choose {|Q_T|-k}}}{{|Q_T| \choose {k}}}.\]
\end{thm}

\begin{theorem}\label{mainthm}
Let $V$ be a Whittaker module for $\mathfrak{g$.  Then $V$ is simple if and only if $\hbox{Wh}\,V$ is $1$-dimensional.
    \end{theorem}

